NumAttr [SimTalk]
Returns the number of user-defined attributes of the object designated by <Path>.
Remarks
The first user-defined attribute has the number 1.
Type
Read-only attribute
Syntax
<Path>.NumAttr
Return Value
The return value has the data type integer.
Is 0 if no user-defined attributes exist.
Example
var index: integer
for index := 1 to MyStation.NumAttr 
    print MyStation.getAttrName(index)
next
See also
User-defined Attributes [general description]
New [user-defined attribute]
