RootFrame [SimTalk]
Returns the root frame of the object designated by <Path>.
Remarks
The root frame is the Frame that is located highest up in the hierarchy of Frames. The root frame is always
located in a folder.
Type
Read-only attribute
Syntax
<Path>.RootFrame → object
Return Value
The return value has the data type object.
VOID if no root frame for the object exists. This applies to all classes that are not of type Frame.
Example
print MyDialog.RootFrame 
// might return .Models.Model
RootFrame [SimTalk]
